1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,455
Cross your fingers
and get two noses?

2
00:00:04,505 --> 00:00:06,525
Stretch out your index and middle fingers

3
00:00:06,575 --> 00:00:08,575
Cross your middle finger
over your index finger

4
00:00:08,625 --> 00:00:12,325
Close your eyes and gently rub
the tip of your nose between the fingertips

5
00:00:12,375 --> 00:00:15,325
Eyes closed, rub gently

6
00:00:15,375 --> 00:00:18,325
How many nose tips do you feel?

7
00:00:18,375 --> 00:00:22,325
Two… noses?!

8
00:00:22,375 --> 00:00:24,395
Uncross your fingers and touch again?

9
00:00:24,445 --> 00:00:27,765
Back to one nose!

10
00:00:27,815 --> 00:00:29,935
The outer side of the index finger and of the middle finger
normally face opposite ways

11
00:00:29,985 --> 00:00:32,305
Touching both at once
= there must be two objects

12
00:00:32,355 --> 00:00:34,305
But when you cross your fingers,
the two outer sides face each other

13
00:00:34,355 --> 00:00:36,475
One nose touches
both outer sides at once

14
00:00:36,525 --> 00:00:40,445
Your brain doesn't know they're crossed,
so it reads "two"

15
00:00:40,495 --> 00:00:42,695
Careful not to poke your eye!

16
00:00:42,745 --> 00:00:45,195
NEXT: Two pencils —
one point or two?
